1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,882
Forces have both size and direction, so we draw them as arrows.

2
00:00:03,882 --> 00:00:09,949
In a tug of war, if both sides pull with 5 newtons in opposite directions, the forces are balanced.

3
00:00:09,949 --> 00:00:15,105
Counting one direction as positive, the resultant force is 5 minus 5, which is zero,

4
00:00:15,105 --> 00:00:16,683
and the rope doesn't move.

5
00:00:17,743 --> 00:00:20,716
Balanced forces don't change an object's motion.

6
00:00:20,716 --> 00:00:24,902
A lorry at constant speed has its engine force balanced by friction.

7
00:00:24,902 --> 00:00:28,845
And when a skydiver's air resistance equals the pull of gravity,

8
00:00:28,845 --> 00:00:32,060
he falls at a steady speed called the terminal speed.

9
00:00:33,121 --> 00:00:37,610
Two paper cones have the same mass, but one is much wider than the other.

10
00:00:37,610 --> 00:00:43,494
They are dropped together from the same height. Predict: which will land first? Pause and decide.

11
00:00:44,555 --> 00:00:48,680
Watch. Both cones start to fall, and air pushes up against each one.

12
00:00:49,741 --> 00:00:54,108
The small cone lands first. The large cone falls slowly and lands later.

13
00:00:55,169 --> 00:00:59,597
Explain what you saw. Both cones have the same weight pulling them down.

14
00:00:59,597 --> 00:01:05,179
The large cone has a bigger surface area, so there is more air resistance pushing up on it.

15
00:01:05,179 --> 00:01:11,609
The forces on it become balanced at a lower speed, so it falls more slowly. Parachutes use the same idea.

16
00:01:11,609 --> 00:01:13,975
Pause and explain it in your own words.

17
00:01:15,035 --> 00:01:19,646
If the forces don't cancel out, they're unbalanced, and the motion changes.

18
00:01:19,646 --> 00:01:25,348
Push a ball right with 12 newtons and left with 5 newtons: the resultant force is 12 minus 5,

19
00:01:25,348 --> 00:01:29,413
which is 7 newtons to the right. The ball accelerates to the right.

20
00:01:30,473 --> 00:01:36,965
Here's a worked example. A box has 100 newtons and 50 newtons pushing right, and 180 newtons pushing left.

21
00:01:36,965 --> 00:01:40,786
Counting right as positive: 100 plus 50 minus 180 is minus 30.

22
00:01:40,786 --> 00:01:45,215
So the resultant force is 30 newtons to the left, and the box moves left.

23
00:01:46,275 --> 00:01:51,129
Unbalanced forces can speed things up, like a car accelerating; slow them down,

24
00:01:51,129 --> 00:01:56,710
like friction stopping a sliding book; or change their direction, like a bat hitting a ball.

25
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:00,804
Air resistance grows with speed and surface area,

26
00:02:00,804 --> 00:02:04,868
so streamlined shapes and lower speeds help vehicles use less fuel.
